# One truth, one owner

Each business fact has a single owner. Do not create a second service, fallback, or UI path that becomes a parallel authority.

UI may code experience: layout, reusable components, interaction, responsive behavior, generic renderers.

UI must not hardcode business truth: product fields, materials, formulas, pricing, costs, readiness, dependencies, module activation, business statuses, totals, commercial flows, or Product Truth.

Do not build a standalone calculator and a separate full-product calculator for the same component. The same geometry, resources, formulas, and technical truth apply in isolation and in composition.

Unselected module = silent. Selected module = independently validatable and calculable, and owns or receives all required truth.

Adjustable technical values live in Product System component settings, not in documentation, Intake, or anonymous code literals. See `docs/architecture/PRODUCT_SYSTEM_TECHNICAL_SETTINGS_CANON.md`.
